 #Findings and Observations
•	Multiple protocol layers work together in common network activities.
•	DNS queries occur before HTTP/HTTPS connections to resolve domain names.
•	TCP establishes reliable connections using a 3-way handshake.
•	HTTP transfers web content in clear text (unless encrypted with TLS).
•	ICMP packets show successful request-reply communication.
This demonstrates how common protocols interact during typical internet usage.
